The memcmp can fail because of implicit function declarations.  The
core issue seems to be that HAVE_STRING_H is not defined.  This is
likely because AC_CHECK_HEADERS is used in a shell conditional branch.
Fixing this properly requires rewriting configure.in and re-running
autoconf, which does not seem worth it.

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index d2ba794b2ede48b4..fb24db5ccf85891c 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -4570,6 +4570,7 @@ else $as_nop
   cat confdefs.h - <<_ACEOF >conftest.$ac_ext
 /* end confdefs.h.  */
 $ac_includes_default
+#include <string.h>
 int
 main (void)
 {
